{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452240-deed-names","id":452240,"title":"Deed-names","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-21T20:39:02-07:00","id":452240,"title":"Deed-names","content":"Given how often the concept of deed-names comes up*, I'm surprised at how little they are talked about in the 2e book. I just ran a search and the phrase comes up once, and then it was just to say that Bone Shadows list them off when gathering. There's no discussion of them being a thing in the greater Uratha culture, nor is there anything about how one gets one.<br /> Was the concept dropped entirely in this edition? If so, I'm curious as to why that was.<br /> <br /> <br /> *several to most of the stories in the Idigam Chronical Anthology feature or talk about them, most of the characters I've seen mentioned in passing here on the forums have them, two of the three wolves in Chris' game have them and the other is specifically called out as not having one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:39:39-07:00","id":454181,"title":"","content":"Did people use Deed-Names when playing first edition Werewolf? How did you like that aspect of the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:38:51-07:00","id":454396,"title":"","content":"A quick perusal of the npc's in the Hunting Grounds chapter sorta confirms the rarity of deed names. I suppose when spirits carve Renown into your soul, deed names might be redundant. Still, it's a useful world-building technique, and I'm willing to bet that there's a few among the Blood Talons and Storm Lords who put a high value on such things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:52:57-07:00","id":454427,"title":"","content":"It probably remains, just exists as something they couldn't elaborate on due to word count.<br /> <br /> When you're introducing a character to someone who in the know, it makes sense you'd still rely on a more Earthly identity. The deed names make more sense as a wolf and Hisil thing, something your totem and other spirits in the area might call you. A name the beshilu might fear or know means a pushover. I have one for my character but so far everyone's called him by his 'real' name.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure renown brands were carved into you in first edition similarly to how they are now, I don't think that's changed much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:13:28-07:00","id":454449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452240-deed-names?p=454181#post454181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did people use Deed-Names when playing first edition Werewolf? How did you like that aspect of the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Consistently... and we absolutely loved this aspect.<br /> <br /> My Favorites from our game are:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Fang-Banger</b></i>: Iron Master Irraka<br /> <i><b>Parts the Veil</b></i>: Bone Shadow Itheaur<br /> <i><b>Wyrd Skinner</b></i>: Hunter in Darkness Cahalith","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:15:51-07:00","id":454541,"title":"","content":"Did Wyrd Skinner have a penchant for hunting down Changelings?<br /> I know that's something Hunters in Darkness are particularly good at now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:47:38-07:00","id":454738,"title":"","content":"I am a huge fan of Deed Names and I was actually a little disappointed with how absent they were in the book, but there were enough at least that the concept hasn't been outright removed, just given a lot less importance. <br /> <br /> I especially like when deed names are actually earned in game, though I've only ever done that once (Stares Down the Storm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:39:03-07:00","id":455254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452240-deed-names?p=454541#post454541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Wyrd Skinner have a penchant for hunting down Changelings?<br /> I know that's something Hunters in Darkness are particularly good at now...</div> </div> </div> </div>On Occasion (he was pretty good at it)... He was feared throughout San Francisco, by all the various Supernaturals. His original Deed Name was &quot;Stalks the Night&quot; but after he killed a powerful Changeling, he earned his new Deed Name. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T21:48:38-07:00","id":457762,"title":"","content":"In a game on this forum I'm going to be playing a Cahalith, I hope I get the chance to actually tell my pack's story to the Lunes, and maybe even *give* them their deed-names myself. How cool would that be, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (unless they didn't like the name, so y'know, we'd just use the edit button...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T07:51:31-07:00","id":458057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452240-deed-names?p=457762#post457762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game on this forum I'm going to be playing a Cahalith, I hope I get the chance to actually tell my pack's story to the Lunes, and maybe even *give* them their deed-names myself. How cool would that be, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (unless they didn't like the name, so y'know, we'd just use the edit button...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Deed Names, much like nick-names, are not always enjoyed by their recipient. Take <i><b>Fang-Banger</b></i>, for instance. He <i>TOTALLY </i>earned that Deed-Name and he regretted it ever after. 500+ Karma in, and he is <i>STILL </i>known as <i><b>Fang Banger</b></i>. But it does give him some recognition and respect among the Vampiric population, as well as many of the other Supernaturals. The fact that he is the Alpha of the most powerful Werewolf Pack in the city might have something to do with it, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-26-2015, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T09:13:26-07:00","id":458095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452240-deed-names?p=458057#post458057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deed Names, much like nick-names, are not always enjoyed by their recipient. Take <i><b>Fang-Banger</b></i>, for instance. He <i>TOTALLY </i>earned that Deed-Name and he regretted it ever after. 500+ Karma in, and he is <i>STILL </i>known as <i><b>Fang Banger</b></i>. But it does give him some recognition and respect among the Vampiric population, as well as many of the other Supernaturals. The fact that he is the Alpha of the most powerful Werewolf Pack in the city might have something to do with it, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not WoD, but related: my Street Samurai's Street Name in Shadowrun is <b><i>Facepalm</i></b>. She's not getting rid of it. She started doing that thing where you own up to your nickname and wear it as a symbol of pride. It's helped somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:30:36-07:00","id":458402,"title":"","content":"I'm sure spreading around the idea that a certain parkouring Irakka should be called 'Batgirl' or 'Bounces McGee' will give plenty of opportunities for owning up to it. Maybe not so much a symbol of pride, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}